## 3. Technical Stack Consistency
| Component | Technology |
|------------|-------------|
| **Language** | TypeScript (JS) |
| **Framework** | Next.js |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL |
| **ORM** | Prisma |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS *(optional)* |
| **Editor** | Tiptap |
| **Icons** | lucide-icon *(use only when absolutely necessary)* |
| **Auth** | Lucia |
| **File Storage** | Vercel Blob |
| **Validation** | Zod |

> These technologies define the official structure of Studio_bada projects.
> All changes or replacements require prior approval from Junseo.
> Consistency and efficiency must always be prioritized.

---

## 4. Design Policy
- Every Studio_bada product must follow the **divetobada.com visual framework**.
- Maintain the same typography, spacing, hierarchy, and component patterns.
- **Icons should be avoided** whenever possible.
- UI or animation changes must be reviewed before implementation.
- No arbitrary or aesthetic-only edits are allowed.

---

## 5. Version Control & Data Management
- Never execute `git clean -fdx`.
- Always run `git clean -n` first if absolutely required.
- Keep backup folders (`backups/`) outside the project directory or in cloud storage.
- Never apply migrations to the production database.
  - All experiments must use a **local or sandboxed database** only.

---

## 6. Learning from Past Failures

### 6.1 2025-01-16 작업물 손실 사건
**원인:**
- 사용자가 "프로젝트를 완전 손상시킴"이라고 표현했을 때, 이는 되돌리기 요청이 아니라 문제 보고였음
- 제가 즉시 `git checkout -- .`를 실행하여 모든 작업물을 삭제함
- 백업 없이 되돌리기를 실행함

**교훈:**
- "손상되었다"는 표현은 문제 보고일 뿐, 되돌리기 요청이 아님
- 되돌리기 전에 반드시 백업 생성
- 사용자가 명시적으로 "되돌려라"고 말하지 않는 한, 되돌리지 말 것
- 문제 해결을 우선 시도할 것

**재발 방지책:**
- Section 2.2, 2.3, 2.4에 명시된 절차를 반드시 준수
- 되돌리기 명령어 실행 전에 항상 백업 생성
- 사용자 확인 없이 되돌리기 실행 금지

- Past mistakes recorded in reflection logs (`worklog_YYYY-MM-DD.md`) are considered **binding lessons**.
- The model should use those reflections to prevent recurrence,
  but must **not replicate failed structures or temporary fixes**.
- Reference: *"작업복기_2025-10-07.md" (Oct 7, 2025)* contains critical lessons regarding layout mismanagement, honesty in reporting, and safe git practices.
  These principles are integrated into this document.

